.TH IMPROV-FORMAT 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-format \- Set how a measure\*(Aqs numbers are shown
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov format\fR <db> <measure> <format>...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set how a measure\*(Aqs numbers are shown.
.PP
The format is general (as many digits as the value needs) or a count of decimals, 0 to 15, then grouped for thousands separators: format m.db Revenue 2 grouped. Decimals round half away from zero; the separators follow IMPROV_LOCALE. show, eval and stream print the measure\*(Aqs cells in it, and the GUI and TUI show it; the values, list and the exports are untouched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fImeasure\fR>
A measure: its numeric id, or its name (all digits is an id)
.TP
<\fIformat\fR>
general, or 0 to 15 decimals, then grouped
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1).
